<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert of Thourotte</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1246</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert of Thourotte was prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Liège from 1240 to 1246, after serving as bishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/langres">Langres</a>. Persuaded by the visions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juliana-of-cornillon">Juliana of Cornillon</a>, he instituted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corpus-christi-feast">Feast of Corpus Christi</a> in his diocese in 1246, the first celebration of a feast later adopted by the whole church.</p></div>
